extraction_notes: |
  - Read from the OCR cache of a scan and verified line by line against a 200
    dpi render of printed 29, which carries the entire entry.
  - THE RANGE IS PRINTED 29 ALONE, NOT THE SURVEY''S 29-31. The entry begins
    below the Time Master''s Cybernetics line in the left column of 29 and ends
    with its own Cybernetics line at the foot of the right column of the same
    page. Printed 30 is a FULL-PAGE ILLUSTRATION - the render shows the folio 30
    at the bottom and nothing but art above it; the "72" in the OCR of that page
    is engraving noise, not a folio. Printed 31 opens the Second Stage
    Promethean, which the book labels Non-Player Characters. So the illustration
    splits nothing: this entry is complete on one page, and the printed-47 trap
    from #415 does not repeat here.
  - PRINTED 29 CARRIES TWO COMPLETE STANDARD EQUIPMENT / MONEY / CYBERNETICS
    TRIPLES. "Money: 2D6x1000 credits" at the top of the page is the Promethean
    Time Master''s; this class''s is the "Money: 2D4x1000 credits" at the bottom,
    with the Phase Mystic O.C.C. heading between them. Read off the render, not
    off a field-source window, which would have shown both inside one span.
  - THE PHASE POWERS ARE CATALOGUED, AS PSIONIC POWERS IN A NEW CATEGORY named
    Phase, from printed 32-35. Printed 32 opens "Phase powers seem to be a
    variation on psionic abilities. Like psionic powers, they are activated by
    using I.S.P.", and names this O.C.C. as the only non-promethean that can
    learn them. Each of the fifteen prints Range, Duration, I.S.P. and a
    description, which is the column set psionic_powers holds; the category
    select in js/catalog-fields.js carries allowOther with a comment saying a
    later book may add a category the core four do not cover.
  - F10 DOES NOT TOUCH THIS CLASS, AND THAT WAS CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSUMED.
    combineClasses keeps whichever psionics block is strictly the higher tier,
    which loses the O.C.C.''s block on a tie. Of the five races this class may
    come from, three - draconid, space wolfen and seljuk - carry no psionics
    block at all, the noro is a major psionic, and human is no race row; this
    class is a master psionic and wins every one of those. The two promethean
    O.C.C.s are the ones that lose, because their own race is a master too.
  - The +3D6 S.D.C. is a pool bonus, cumulative on whatever the race brings. The
    book''s alternative - +3D6 M.D.C. for a mystic who is already an M.D.C.
    being - is conditional on the race and so cannot be a class bonus; it is on
    the Trained Physique ability instead. The +1 to P.S. and +1 to P.P. are
    flat numbers and are stored as bonuses.
  - THIS LIST IS NOT THE PHASE ADEPT''S, AND TEN LINES DIFFER. Eight are in the
    O.C.C. skills: Trade Two against Native Language, two languages of choice at
    +25% against three at +20%, Advanced Math +20% against +10%, Galactic Lore
    +15% against +10%, Pilot: Small Spacecraft +20% against +15%, Pilot: any two
    +15% against +10%, Prowl +15% against +10%, and Hand to Hand: Martial Arts
    against Expert. Two are in the related list: Pilot Related +10% against +5%,
    and Wilderness +5% against no bonus at all. The secondary count differs as
    well, four against six. Counted line by line off the two renders, because
    the ten lines they share word for word are what makes the other ten easy to
    copy across.
  - Attribute requirements: I.Q. and M.E. 15 or higher. "High physical
    attributes are desirable but not necessary" is advice, not a minimum, and is
    not stored.
  - Standard Equipment: the steelcloth robes and jumpsuit are A.R. 19 and 40
    M.D.C. and are added to the gear catalog by this batch - a DIFFERENT item
    from the Phase Adept''s steelcloth robes, which are A.R. 12 and 90 M.D.C.
    The book names and stats both. The heavy environmental body armor
    "appropriate for the race" carries no figure at all here, unlike the Phase
    Adept''s 150 M.D.C., so it is a choice among the armors this book does stat.
---

## Lore

A few worthy non-prometheans with great psionic potential are sometimes accepted
as pupils by the phase adepts. This tiny elite are the only creatures besides
the promethean race with any degree of control over phase powers - not as
extensive or as great as a true adept''s, and without the special powers of the
promethean race, but enough that phase mystics are widely feared. Even limited
phase abilities make a fearsome enemy.

Phase mystics undergo the same training and initiation rituals as phase adepts,
and are expected to follow the same code of honor and strict morality and to
champion the cause of good wherever they go. Sometimes one turns against his
former teachers and becomes a powerful criminal or conqueror, which is a large
part of why so few beings are ever taught the secrets of phase powers at all.

The lucky few who do learn them usually become dedicated enemies of evil,
joining forces with cosmo-knights and other champions. Others remove themselves
from human concerns entirely and concentrate on mastering their powers. Despite
what they can do, phase mystics are as baffled by phase technology as anybody
else.

## GM Notes

Force fields stop most phase powers, teleportation included, and magic barriers
hinder or stop them. Most magic spells and weapons inflict FULL damage on a
phase mystic, the same as on a first stage promethean - it is the second stagers
who take half. A phase mystic who abuses the powers draws bounty hunters,
mercenaries, cosmo-knights and prometheans down on him.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'phase-mystic');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'phase-mystic';
SELECT count(*) AS stub_gear FROM gear WHERE slug IN ('steelcloth-robes-and-jumpsuit', 'meditation-chip');

